# ============================================================
# Files that must never reach the web root.
#
# _htaccess had a rule refusing to serve these. That rule does nothing
# on Vercel, and a "deny" rule is the weaker answer anyway: the file
# is still sitting on the host, one misconfiguration away from being
# readable. Not deploying it at all has no such failure mode.
#
# deploy-schema.sql holds the entire database design — every table,
# every RLS policy, every function grant, and the note explaining
# which RPCs are deliberately reachable by anon. That is a map.
#
# The email-*.html files are templates for pasting into Supabase →
# Authentication → Emails. They are not pages and render as broken
# markup with {{ .ConfirmationURL }} showing through.
# ============================================================

deploy-schema.sql
email-confirm-signup.html
email-reset-password.html

# Build-time script only — reads the seven pages and rewrites their
# CSP connect-src. Nothing at runtime calls it.
sync-csp.js

# Apache config, inert here. vercel.json is what this host reads.
_htaccess

.git
node_modules
*.md
